infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Three production bundle rescues — every fix was structural, never "compress more"
  desc Pinterest, Tinder, and Stripe each shipped too much code to the wrong route; the win came from split, lazy, or replace — not from minifying harder
  lists
    - label Pinterest 2017 — split the bundle
      desc One large bundle blocked the main thread for 12 s. Rewriting it into per-route chunks, so each page loads only its own code, cut bounce rate by 40%.
    - label Tinder 2019 — remove dead weight
      desc An admin panel was bundled into consumer routes that never used it. Deleting that 200 KB of unused code lifted conversion by 5%.
    - label Stripe 2020 — replace and lazy-load
      desc Stripe.js shipped 80 KB up front on every checkout. Swapping it for a small loader that lazy-loads the full library cut time-to-interactive by 35%.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
